def f(num,title,body,ev,action,validation='Full source-body review; no retained program or historical command executed.',severity='medium'):return {'id':f'OPSKILL-F{num:03}','severity':severity,'title':title,'finding':body,'evidence':ev,'recommended_action':action,'validation':validation}
rows=[
f(42,'Git safety hook is a fail-open lexical filter','The hook checks unanchored literal-like regexes after jq extraction without checking parse/tool failure. git -C repo push origin main evades every pattern; missing jq or malformed JSON can leave an empty command and exit 0. Quoted documentation can match despite no Git operation. The guide promises all push variants.',[e(146,7,17),e(151,3,25)],'Use validated structured inputs and a shell-aware command boundary; refuse parse/tool errors, explicitly cover global options and limit claims to supported syntax.','CHECK-030 is an in-memory regex counterexample; Git and Bash were not launched.','high'),
f(43,'Lock-file age/size and force teardown are insufficient preservation proofs','The recovery reference defines stale as zero bytes plus unchanged mtime over two checks, but a live Git operation may legitimately hold that same lock unchanged. Another recipe force-removes a worktree after inspecting only committed diff, which excludes untracked/unstaged work. These shortcuts conflict with the later clean-status preservation protocol.',[e(147,268,287),e(147,306,308),e(147,694,704),e(150,556,575)],'Require process/owner coordination and independently preserved recovery state; prefer refusal/non-forced removal when dirty or ownership is unknown. Do not infer liveness from mtime alone.'),
f(44,'Selective-landing recipes confuse endpoint differences with merge deletion and supersession','A branch lacking a file added later on main yields ONLY_MAIN in a two-dot tree diff, but a three-way merge normally retains that file. Similarly, resolving every conflict to main before checking for an empty diff can erase genuine conflicting PR changes by construction. Comparing one commit touched paths cannot prove all earlier branch commits landed.',[e(147,579,591),e(148,16,19),e(150,467,479),e(150,812,825)],'Use pinned merge-base authored deltas and actual prospective merge trees; assess conflicting intent before choosing main, and enumerate every branch-only commit/path before declaring supersession.'),
f(45,'Idempotence alone does not make residual norm the true L1 distance','The quotient skill states ||x-Cx||1 is the true L1 quotient distance for idempotent endomorphisms. C=[[1,2],[0,0]] is idempotent, but x=(0,1) gives residual norm 3 while its distance to im(C), the x-axis, is 1. The formula can define a projector-dependent diagnostic but not the claimed general minimum.',[e(158,16,24)],'State the quotient and norm precisely. Require a proven metric projection property or solve/certify the minimum independently; retain the residual as a separate diagnostic.','CHECK-031 verifies the exact matrix and distances.','high'),
f(46,'Static inward-dependency resolver drops imported submodule aliases','When ImportFrom.module is present, import_targets returns only the module name. Thus from pkg import infrastructure omits the outer-layer alias and passes, unlike import pkg.infrastructure. The top-level scanner also treats an empty discovered domain population as PASS and the single-root check only looks for applications.',[e(160,17,32),e(162,17,34),e(163,60,85),e(163,133,151)],'Resolve imported names against known module/package inventory, declare dynamic-import limits, require expected scan population and cover every declared layer root.','CHECK-032 reproduces the missing alias using Python AST only.'),
f(47,'Exact-solver documentation mixes missing evidence with obstruction and overstates attainment argument','The main skill maps missing problem data to OPEN_OBSTRUCTION, while its reference correctly says missing evidence must be UNAVAILABLE/refusal and positive obstruction needs a witness. The main skill also appeals to compactness/extreme vertices of unrestricted real potentials, but gauge translations make that domain noncompact and leave lineality unless quotient/gauge fixing is supplied.',[e(168,28,32),e(170,10,28)],'Use one typed unavailable terminal; separately state finite graph, positive weights, gauge fixing/quotient coercivity and rational inputs for the spanning-forest attainment argument. Do not present the hard-coded triangle script as a general solver test.'),
f(48,'Finite algebra validator rubric incorrectly requires all categories and monoids to be groupoids','The relational reference groups categories, monoids and groupoids together and mandates inverse maps/laws for every morphism. General categories and monoids need not have inverses. Nonempty carrier is likewise an additional policy for categories, not a general categorical axiom.',[e(169,140,152)],'Split category/monoid/group/groupoid contracts and test the exact selected axioms; record nonemptiness as an explicit admission when required.','CHECK-036 checks a finite category A->B with identities and no inverse for its nonidentity arrow.'),
f(49,'Governance verification commands certify much less than their prose and PASS labels','Release checker searches one zero-hash string and never examines staging or recomputes digests; Lean checker only recognizes a toolchain prefix and never builds or inspects axioms; literature checker accepts any YAML mapping and never reconciles indices. Each is presented as verification of substantially broader invariants.',[e(172,17,32),e(173,12,44),e(177,17,38),e(178,12,43),e(179,17,31),e(180,14,42)],'Name each command and terminal by its implemented predicate; add separate bound substantive checks and report unavailable obligations rather than aggregate verification.','CHECK-033 and CHECK-034 show invalid toolchain suffix and undetected digest forms; source review shows no relevant execution paths.','high'),
f(50,'Unit-backed Lean structure destroys the promised representation opacity','The Lean skill suggests structure T where carrier : Unit := () as an opaque abstract carrier substitute. This constructs a concrete inhabited singleton, exposing its representation and collapsing all instances; it cannot represent an arbitrary Vector6 or preserve intended domain cardinality. Explicit domain-contract hypotheses do not undo that carrier restriction.',[e(177,25,30)],'Use a parameterized carrier with explicit Nonempty/Inhabited assumptions or a genuine concrete vector representation; state imported assumptions and prove inhabitedness without replacing the domain by Unit.'),
f(51,'Pedagogy discovery can omit malformed categorized tracks and assertion presence is weak','Categorized discovery occurs only if both notebooks and concepts directories exist. A numbered track with only concepts falls into legacy discovery, which only admits children already containing a matching notebook, so its missing companions can disappear from the census while other tracks keep strict nonzero count. Assertion detection also accepts assert 1 and unreachable assertions.',[e(181,19,30),e(187,94,140),e(187,221,253),e(187,273,302)],'Classify layout from an explicit declaration or any categorized marker, report missing required directories before fallback, and keep syntactic assertion counts distinct from executed mutation-sensitive checks.','CHECK-035 exercises the exact AST predicate on synthetic strings; discovery omission established by complete branch review.'),
f(52,'Governance contracts retain conflicting live output, host and publication policies','Git main says never squash while linked playbooks prefer squash; councils require a red-team Markdown output while core-red-team mandates JSONL only; host-parity uses tracked roster while declared-vs-actual insists filesystem discovery is authoritative. These are active sibling contracts, not merely two unexecuted historical examples.',[e(145,78,85),e(147,393,406),e(164,108,114),e(118,86,88),e(174,15,22),e(120,45,53)],'Select one current contract per boundary and fence earlier variants as history, with explicit compatibility/version mappings instead of contradictory mandatory rules.'),
f(53,'Pedagogy exactness and proof tags need narrower mathematical carriers','Scaffolding requires all cochain/eigenvalue calculations use Fraction, but rational matrices can have irrational eigenvalues, e.g. [[0,2],[1,0]] has roots of lambda^2-2. The claim legend also overloads Proved between kernel proof and finite Python execution, while another reference mandates a different eight-tag taxonomy.',[e(183,37,43),e(182,9,16),e(184,75,80)],'Permit exact algebraic/symbolic carriers where rationals are not closed under the operation; distinguish Formal, finite Executed/Tested and Declared without overloading Proved.')
]
